 in 1996. Though many of the smaller awards have been discontinued over the years, the PEN Translation Prize and PEN Award for Poetry in Translation ... \",\"title\":\"https://pen.org/literary-awards/literary-awards-history/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... Laurea honoris causa (honorary degree), Italian Language and Literature, University of Siena for Foreigners, Italy, 2015\\n\\n- Honorary Doctor of Letters, Williams College, 2005\\n\\n- Honorary Doctor of Humane Letters, University of Rhode Island, 2001\\n\\nLITERARY AWARDS & CITATIONS\\n\\n- The John Florio Prize for translation into English from Italian, 2021\\n\\n- Named ... \",\"title\":\"https://barnard.edu/profiles/jhumpa-lahiri\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... Translations aren't allowed unless a poet translates their own work.\\n\\nWord count: 40 lines\\n\\nPrize: $20,000 CAD\\n\\nEntry fee: $25\\n\\nClosing date: 15 May 2024\\n\\nThis poetry competition awards one poem with publication in The American Poetry Review. All entrants receive a copy of the magazine ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.papertrue.com/blog/writing-contests-2024/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d7\"},\"ref\":\"d7\",\"snippet\":\" ... It was also awarded France's Prix Femina for a work in translation. Her seventh novel, Someone, was a New York Times bestseller, a finalist for the Dublin IMPAC Award, the National Book Critics Circle Award, the Patterson Prize for Fiction, and the Dayton Literary Peace Prize. Three ... \",\"title\":\"https://missionandministry.georgetown.edu/conference-participants/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d8\"},\"ref\":\"d8\",\"snippet\":\" ... over, who have a history of publication in creative writing. Genre: Short fiction. Prize: £15,000 to the winner, £3,000 for the runner-up and £500 for three further shortlisted writers. Deadline: March 17, 2025.\\n\\nAmerican Literary Translators Association Italian Prose in Translation Award. Genre: Translation of ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishedtodeath.blogspot.com/2025/02/77-free-writing-contests-in-march-2025.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d9\"},\"ref\":\"d9\",\"snippet\":\" ... Now living in Montreal, she works as a language professional in cinema, education, and literary translation. Arielle translated 21 Days in October a YA novel by Magali Favre.\\n\\nPeter McCambridge is a full-time, award-winning literary translator. Originally from Ireland, Peter holds a BA in modern languages ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.barakabooks.com/authors/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d10\"},\"ref\":\"d10\",\"snippet\":\" ... Marie-Aude Murail has a gift for creating characters that have a special bond with the reader. Her novels explore various themes of politics, history, love, adventure and fantasy and have been translated into more than 22 languages. She has been awarded most French prizes in the field ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ibby.org/subnavigation/archives/hans-christian-andersen-awards/2020\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"39eb57c3908f1c4bce4d1542b0e4ca245c998bd93abe3dddc4df3bfb96915c83\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"b029843b975816a0b572cf272525715c969cb4082dbe63bcb5f0746b393488d4\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"literary award created 2000s translated over 25 languages\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d11\"},\"ref\":\"d11\",\"snippet\":\" ... Established by Barbara Kingsolver in 2000 and funded entirely by her, it is awarded biennially to the author of a previously unpublished novel of high literary caliber that exemplifies the prize's founding principles.\\n\\nThe PEN/Faulkner Award for Fiction is a national prize which honors the best ... \",\"title\":\"https://americanwritersmuseum.org/literary-links/literary-awards/?srsltid=AfmBOooYIGTV-EUbGd9xDLmBUtcV_Ts9VM7oqhh4K0lfwTLcUoKmITFg\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d1\"},\"ref\":\"d1\",\"snippet\":\" ... See also\\n\\n* Baillie Gifford Prize (formerly the Samuel Johnson Prize)\\n* Commonwealth Writers Prize\\n* Costa Book Awards\\n* German Book Prize (Deutscher Buchpreis)\\n* Giller Prize (known as the Scotiabank Giller Prize from 2005 to 2023)\\n* Governor General's Awards\\n* Grand Prix of Literary Associations\\n* Miles Franklin Award\\n* Prix Goncourt\\n* Russian ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d12\"},\"ref\":\"d12\",\"snippet\":\" ... Top prizes range from $300 to $2000.\\n\\nLush Triumphant Literary Awards\\n\\nThe awards, offered by subTerrain, are for fiction, poetry, and nonfiction. The cost to enter is $30 and awards $3000 in prizes.\\n\\nMarilyn Baillie Picture Book Award\\n\\nThis award honours excellence in the picture book format. Awarded ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.dreamerswriting.com/writing-contests-in-canada/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d13\"},\"ref\":\"d13\",\"snippet\":\" ... Books Abroad International Prize for Literature before changing to its current name in 1976. The award recognizes outstanding works in drama, poetry, and fiction.\\n\\nNotable winners: Gabriel Garcia Marquez (1972); Czesław Miłosz (1978)\\n\\n6. Women's Prize for Fiction\\n\\nThe Women's Prize for Fiction awards were established ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.tckpublishing.com/prestigious-literature-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... Book prizes remained relatively scarce until the 1940s; but since the second half of the twentieth century, the number of literary prizes has grown dramatically. Today, there are literally thousands of national and international awards for literature. An author who writes a novel sitting at her desk in ... \",\"title\":\"https://giramondopublishing.com/heat/archive/beth-driscoll-how-prizes-work-in-the-literary-economy/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1935\\n\\nThe is a Japanese literary award presented biannually. Because of its prestige and the considerable attention the winner receives from the media, it is, along with the Naoki Prize, one of Japan's most sought after literary prizes.\\n\\nHistory\\n\\nThe Akutagawa Prize was established in 1935 by ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akutagawa_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... Poetry Prize\\n\\nAwarded annually to one Canadian and one international poet or translator. It is based on their work from the previous year. The prize is named after Scott Griffin and was established in 2000.\\n\\nRecent Winners\\n\\nprevious Winners (2023)\\n\\nWorking towards a major book award is a ... \",\"title\":\"https://rocketexpansion.com/book-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d17\"},\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... National Book Award – Blonde\\\"National Book Awards – 2000\\\". NBF. Retrieved April 14, 2014.\\n* 2000: Bram Stoker Award (Long Fiction) - In Shock\\n* 2001: Locus Award (Novelette) - In Shock\\n* 2001: International Horror Guild Award, best Short Fiction, for Angel of Mercy\\n* 2002: Los Angeles Book Prize, Best Young Adult Novel ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joyce_Carol_Oates\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d18\"},\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... Gibb was the winner of the Trillium Book Award in 2006, a Scotiabank Giller Prize short list nominee in 2005, winner of the city of Toronto Book Award in 2000 and the recipient of the CBC Canadian Literary Award for short fiction in 2001. Her books have been ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d19\"},\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... Writing Battle\\n\\nAwards: Prizes vary by battle type\\n\\nEligibility: International; entry fee varies by contest\\n\\nWebsite: writingbattle.com\\n\\nyolk Montreal Fiction Prize\\n\\nAward: $2000 first prize; $500 second & third prize\\n\\nEligibility: Open to all Canadian writers\\n\\nAwards for Young Writers\\n\\nJames Bartleman Indigenous Youth Creative Writing Awards\\n\\nAwards ... \",\"title\":\"https://fireflycreativewriting.com/contests-for-canadian-writers\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"09d38c9db86e5f8af89ed2032d43afc72e09ff21c2c0fb766da925d9d83600ff\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"7e6a427519a6f46075e903a316ac894c53264f479bced8878f407ff3ff7ae482\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"book award established 2000s international literary prize\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d20\"},\"ref\":\"d20\",\"snippet\":\" ... Daniel Halpern was born in Syracuse, New York, grew up in Los Angeles and Seattle, and has lived in Tangier, Morocco, New York City and Princeton. He is the author of nine collections of poetry, most recently Something Shining. For 25 years, Halpern edited the international literary magazine ... \",\"title\":\"https://centerforfiction.org/grants-awards/medal-for-editorial-excellence/medal-for-editorial-excellence-past-recipients/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d18\"},\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... Giller Prize shortlisted - Alligator\\n\\n2003:Winterset Award for Excellence in Newfoundland Writing - Open\\n\\n2002: Giller Prize short-listed - Open\\n\\nCanadian Authors Association Jubilee Award (short fiction)\\n\\nMar 15 Camilla Gibb\\n\\nMar 29 Larissa Lai\\n\\nLarissa Lai was born in California in 1967. She grew up in Newfoundland, and ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.c