"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d24\"},\"ref\":\"d24\",\"snippet\":\" ... Visit: \\n\\n| |\\n\\nJeff Walt | Jeff Walt was born in rural Pennsylvania among a community of coal miners, bricklayers, and railroad workers. His chapbook, Soot, was awarded co-winner of the Keystone Chapbook Prize and published in 2010 by Seven Kitchens Press. He's been awarded writing residencies from The ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.givalpress.com/authors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d25\"},\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... Total prize fund: £6,000.\\n\\nTHE QUEEN'S KNICKERS AWARD WINNER: ELENA AREVALO MELVILLE FOR UMBRELLA (SCALLYWAG PRESS) AWARDED £5,000\\n\\nElena Arevalo Melville grew up in tropical Guatemala, studied architecture in Barcelona, and now lives in Cambridge with her partner and children. She has an MA in ... \",\"title\":\"https://societyofauthors.org/2020/06/18/winners-of-the-2020-society-of-authors-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d10\"},\"ref\":\"d10\",\"snippet\":\" ... for many book prizes. She has lived for short periods in the UK, Hong Kong, Australia and Spain and has travelled widely for speeches, conferences and book fairs.\\n\\nCyprus\\n\\nAnna Kalogirou-Pavlou\\n\\nAnna Kalogirou-Pavlou was born in Kyrenia in 1940 and grew up in nearby Lapithos on ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ibby.org/subnavigation/archives/hans-christian-andersen-awards/2020\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d26\"},\"ref\":\"d26\",\"snippet\":\" ... only four writers ever to win the prize twice. He has also published two books of nonfiction. In 2002, he received a MacArthur Fellowship.\\n\\nEarly life\\n\\nWhitehead was born in New